STEP 1: Remove GitHub credentials from Windows (VERY IMPORTANT)

Open Control Panel
Go to Credential Manager
Click Windows Credentials
Find anything named:
github.com
git:https://github.com
❌ Delete ALL of them


🟢 WAY 1: VS CODE + GIT TERMINAL (BEST & MUST-KNOW)
🔹 STEP 1: Open project folder in VS Code

IMPORTANT
Open the root folder, not individual files.

placement_portal/
├── app.py
├── templates/
├── static/


🔹 STEP 2: Initialize Git (ONLY ONCE)

In terminal:
git init

This creates:
.git/   ← hidden folder


⚠️ Without .git, nothing will track.
🔹 STEP 3: Check file status
git status


You’ll see:
Untracked files:
  templates/
  static/
This means Git sees them but is not tracking yet.

🔹 STEP 4: Add files to Git (TRACK THEM)

Add everything:
git add .
OR specific folder:
git add templates static
Check again:
git status
Now files are staged.

🔹 STEP 5: Commit (SAVE SNAPSHOT)
git commit -m "Initial project structure"


📌 Commit = permanent save point.

🔹 STEP 6: Connect to GitHub (Remote)

Create empty repository on GitHub.

Then:

git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repo-name.git
Verify:
git remote -v

🔹 STEP 7: Push to GitHub
git push -u origin main


🎉 CODE IS NOW ON GITHUB

🔄 HOW CODE UPDATES WORK (VERY IMPORTANT)

Every time you change code:

git status
git add .
git commit -m "what you changed"
git push


👉 If you skip any step → code won’t update

git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Remove venv and add gitignore"
git push

pip freeze > requirements.txt
git add requirements.txt
git commit -m "Add requirements"
git push
